{{also|Cast|čast|část|časť|çast|cast.}}
==English==
{{slim-wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|casten}}, from {{der|en|non|kasta||to throw, cast, overturn}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*kastōną||to throw, cast}}, of unknown origin. 

Cognate with {{cog|sco|cast||to cast, throw}}, {{cog|da|kaste||to throw}}, {{cog|sv|kasta||to throw, cast, fling, toss, discard}}, {{cog|is|kasta||to pitch, toss}}. In the sense of "flinging", displaced native {{m|en|warp}}.

The senses relating to broadcasting are based on that same term; compare [[-cast]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}}: {{enPR|käst}}, {{IPA|en|/kɑːst/}}
* {{a|Northern England}}: {{enPR|kăst}}, {{IPA|en|/kast/}}
* {{a|GA}}: {{enPR|kăst}}, {{IPA|en|/kæst/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-cast.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|caste|karst|q2=in some non-rhotic accents}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːst|æst|s=1}}

