|passage=One copy of the magnificent caveman, The Thinker, of which Rodin '''cast''' several examples in bronze, is seated now in front of the Detroit Museum of Art, where it was placed last autumn.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1944|month=November and December|author=A Former Pupil|title=Some Memories of Crewe Works—II|journal=Railway Magazine|page=343|text=The practice of '''casting''' steel seems the most difficult of all the foundry arts, for despite every care, a percentage of the work is liable to be faulty and disappointing, but at Crewe, generally, a very good class of casting was turned out.}}
## {{lb|en|printing|dated}} To [[stereotype]] or [[electrotype]].
# To [[twist]] or [[warp]] (of fabric, timber etc.). {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=c. 1680|author=w:Joseph Moxon|title=The Art of Joinery
|passage=Stuff is said to '''cast''' or warp when{{...}}it alters its flatness or straightness.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} To bring the [[bow]]s of a [[sailing ship]] on to the required [[tack]] just as the [[anchor]] is [[weighed]] by use of the [[headsail]]; to bring (a ship) round. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
# To [[deposit]] (a ballot or voting paper); to formally register (one's vote). {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} To [[change]] a [[variable]] [[type]] from, for example, [[integer]] to [[real]], or integer to text. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|To display a number, you need to '''cast''' it to a string type.}}
# {{lb|en|hunting}} Of dogs, hunters: to [[spread out]] and [[search]] for a [[scent]]. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1955|author=w:William Golding|title={{w|The Inheritors (William Golding)|The Inheritors}}|publisher=Faber and Faber|year_published=2005|page=50
|passage=He clambered on to an apron of rock that held its area out to the sun and began to '''cast''' across it. The direction of the wind changed and the scent touched him again.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} To [[set]] (a bone etc.) in a cast.
#: {{rfex|en|some are still missing examples}}
# {{lb|en|Wicca}} To open a [[circle]] in order to begin a [[spell]] or meeting of [[witch]]es.
# {{lb|en|media}} To [[broadcast]] (video) over the [[Internet]] or a local network, especially to one's [[television]].
#: {{ux|en|The streamer was the first to '''cast''' footage of the new game.}}

